    "created_at": "2022-08-20T02:52:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-20T02:52:16Z",
    "body": "There's two things going on here: Javascript/WASM's interaction with the browser, and the browser's interaction with the underlying OS.\r\n\r\nFor the former, I expect we'll be moving in the direction of all-sync SyncAccessHandles, since C(++) applications being ported to the web via WASM _largely_ expect a synchronous file API (see the discussion on #7).\r\n\r\nThe latter is really up to the user agent, though of course how we design the API puts constraints on the implementation.\r\n\r\nMy intuition is that as things stand now, getting the former correct is more impactful from a performance perspective than the latter, since it [influences how libraries can be architected](https://github.com/whatwg/fs/issues/7#issuecomment-1219971463). And this is a spec repo so most of the attention you'll see on this forum is on the former :)\r\n\r\n(that being said, I'm intrigued by the performance optimizations suggested in #47)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
