    "created_at": "2022-08-20T03:35:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-20T03:35:42Z",
    "body": "> For the former, I expect we'll be moving in the direction of all-sync SyncAccessHandles, since C(++) applications being ported to the web via WASM _largely_ expect a synchronous file API (see the discussion on #7).\r\n\r\nA synchronous API is okay to start with, but in the long term, the focus should be on asynchronous APIs, as they allow for much improved responsiveness and better use of parallelism.  This is _not_ specific to the web, but rather a consequence of how storage works in general.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
